# Io Moon, the whole game in ONE run, on the parent set `iomoon` at the
# Netherlands country default (SW40-2/3/4 = country 4, English, F11).
#
# Every other walk in walks/iomoon.json captures one area. This one plays a
# complete three-ball game covering the branches that matter, visits the service
# menu, then changes the country DIP live and replays the game in Spanish -- all
# inside a single process, so one dump holds the lot.
#
# Why each ball is what it is:
#
#   BALL 1  MULTIBALL.  The drop bank resets only at ball start (3.3.6) and it
#           selects between the two two-ball-lock modes (3.3.7): standing gives
#           Multiball, flat gives Wonderful Thing. Ball 1 leaves it standing.
#           ORBITS x6 first, because Jupiter retains nothing until the letter
#           count [413C:0102] reaches 6. Then two locks, the shepherding the
#           start needs (below), the Jackpot at bull's-eye 2 and the
#           Superjackpot at Ramp 2, then drain out of the mode.
#
#   BALL 2  WONDERFUL THING -- the Black Hole branch. The bank comes back up at
#           ball start, so this ball flattens it (Z X C V N) before locking.
#           The inner target with the bank already flat starts Special Drop
#           Probe (3.2.7). Two locks with the bank down is Wonderful Thing
#           (3.2.2), whose own shot is Ramp 2: it lights lane 8's extra ball and
#           releases the held balls one after another instead of together.
#
#   BALL 3  THE MONOLITH.  Lane 6 arms it, scoop 1 cashes whatever position is
#           lit at that instant (3.3.3) -- the cycle runs continuously, so the
#           award is whatever it lands on. Then both shooters, which alternate
#           LPA11/LPA12, the Lagrange pair that is never cashed.
#
# The shepherding, which is most of the lock sequences: the Multiball start is a
# chain of blocking waits (F22) and the simulator's keys act on ONE ball at a
# time. `Down` steps to the next ball. sub_DC6AC releases with 0xEE and waits for
# the released ball to report at a SCOOP -- sub_DC675 accepts codes 0x21/0x22 and
# nothing else -- and re-issues 0xEE every five seconds forever if none comes. A
# lane will not answer it.
#
# LANGUAGE. This script is language-neutral -- it presses no key that depends on
# the text on screen -- so the same walk captures the Spanish corpus by running it
# against a country-5 cfg. That is the `full-run-es` walk in walks/iomoon.json,
# and `run_walks.py iomoon --only full-run,full-run-es` captures both.
#
# Changing the country *inside* one run does not work. There is no command-line
# DIP option in this build, so the only lever is MAME's own menu, and a key script
# cannot drive it: nine combinations of DOWN counts into TAB -> Dip Switches ->
# SW40-2/3/4 Country -> RIGHT left the country byte in the written cfg unchanged at
# 8 (country 4) every time, where the Spanish cfg holds 10. The script itself keeps
# running -- marks after the TAB are still written -- and key injection sits at the
# bottom of the input system (`internal_code_pressed`, input.c), so the UI ought to
# see the presses; what is not established is why `input_ui_pressed`'s edge
# detection does not act on them. KEYCODE_F3 (soft reset) DOES work from a key
# script and the dump continues in the same file, so if that edge case is ever
# solved, a single-run language switch becomes possible.
#
# Keys: S lane 4, L lane 6; LCtrl+B bull's-eye 1, RCtrl+B bull's-eye 2;
#       LCtrl+R ramp 1, RCtrl+R ramp 2; LCtrl+H scoop 1; J Jupiter; I inner bank;
#       Z/X/C/V/N drop targets A-E; W/E/D bumpers; O lane 10; Y/U lanes 1/2;
#       LCtrl+- / RCtrl+- shooters; Q drain; Down next ball; Space plunge;
#       7 test/service; LShift scroll, RShift select; 5 coin; 1 start.
    40 tap 8 KEYCODE_1
   500 mark boot

# ---- credit and ball 1 -------------------------------------------------------
  1400 tap 10 KEYCODE_5
  1480 tap 10 KEYCODE_5
  1560 tap 10 KEYCODE_5
  1640 tap 10 KEYCODE_5
  1720 tap 10 KEYCODE_5
  1800 tap 10 KEYCODE_5
  1950 mark credit
  1960 tap 10 KEYCODE_1
  2200 mark ball-1-start
  2210 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
  2450 mark plunged

# general play, for the ordinary in-play screens
  2600 tap 6 KEYCODE_W
  2750 tap 6 KEYCODE_E
  2900 tap 6 KEYCODE_D
  3050 tap 6 KEYCODE_Y
  3200 tap 6 KEYCODE_U
  3350 tap 6 KEYCODE_O
  3550 mark general-play
  3700 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_R
  3900 mark ramp-1

# ORBITS x6 -- lane 4 lights LD1, bull's-eye 1 takes one letter
  4100 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
  4200 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  4300 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
  4400 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  4500 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
  4600 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  4700 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
  4800 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  4900 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
  5000 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  5100 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
  5200 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  5400 mark orbits-complete

# two locks, bank standing -> MULTIBALL
  5600 mark jupiter-lock-1
  5610 tap 10 KEYCODE_J
  5800 mark replacement-ball-1
  5810 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
  5880 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
  6050 mark jupiter-lock-2-multiball
  6060 tap 10 KEYCODE_J
  6260 mark follow-the-released-ball
  6270 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
  6350 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
  6460 mark scoop-1-takes-the-released-ball
  6470 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_H
  6620 mark plunge-the-served-ball
  6630 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
  6720 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
  6790 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
  6870 mark multiball-running
  6880 tap 10 KEYCODE_Y
  7060 mark scoop-1-takes-the-second-released-ball
  7070 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_H
  7260 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
  7460 mark jackpot
  7470 tap 10 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  7760 mark superjackpot
  7770 tap 10 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_R
  8060 mark both-awards-paid

# drain out of Multiball: 3 -> 2 -> 1 ends the mode, the last ends the ball
  8300 tap 10 KEYCODE_Q
  8600 mark two-balls-left
  8610 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
  8700 tap 10 KEYCODE_Q
  9000 mark multiball-over
  9100 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
  9200 tap 10 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
  9400 mark bullseye2-base-value-again
  9600 tap 10 KEYCODE_Q
 10100 mark ball-1-over

# ---- ball 2: the drop bank and WONDERFUL THING (Black Hole) -------------------
 10300 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
 10550 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
 10900 mark ball-2-plunged

# ORBITS again -- the count reset when Multiball ended
 11100 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
 11200 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
 11300 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
 11400 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
 11500 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
 11600 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
 11700 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
 11800 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
 11900 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
 12000 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
 12100 tap 6 KEYCODE_S
 12200 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_B
 12400 mark orbits-complete-again

# flatten the bank, then the inner target -> SPECIAL DROP PROBE
 12600 tap 6 KEYCODE_Z
 12700 tap 6 KEYCODE_X
 12800 tap 6 KEYCODE_C
 12900 tap 6 KEYCODE_V
 13000 tap 6 KEYCODE_N
 13200 mark bank-flat
 13400 tap 6 KEYCODE_I
 13500 mark special-drop-probe
 14300 mark probe-expired

# two locks with the bank DOWN -> WONDERFUL THING
 14500 mark wonderful-lock-1
 14510 tap 10 KEYCODE_J
 14700 mark wonderful-replacement
 14710 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
 14790 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
 14980 mark wonderful-thing-lock-2
 14990 tap 10 KEYCODE_J
 15250 mark wonderful-thing-running
 15260 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
 15340 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
 15450 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_H
 15650 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
 15900 mark black-hole-ramp-2
 15910 tap 10 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_R
 16200 mark ramp-2-in-wonderful-thing
 16400 tap 10 KEYCODE_PERIOD
 16650 mark lane-8-extra-ball
 17000 tap 10 KEYCODE_Q
 17400 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
 17500 tap 10 KEYCODE_Q
 17900 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
 18000 tap 10 KEYCODE_Q
 18600 mark ball-2-over

# ---- ball 3: the Monolith ----------------------------------------------------
 18800 tap 10 KEYCODE_DOWN
 19050 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
 19400 mark ball-3-plunged
 19600 tap 6 KEYCODE_L
 19800 mark monolith-armed-1
 19900 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_H
 20200 mark monolith-cashed-1
 20500 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
 20800 tap 6 KEYCODE_L
 21000 mark monolith-armed-2
 21100 tap 10 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_H
 21400 mark monolith-cashed-2
 21700 tap 40 KEYCODE_SPACE
 22000 tap 6 KEYCODE_LCONTROL,KEYCODE_MINUS
 22200 mark lagrange-shooter-1
 22400 tap 6 KEYCODE_RCONTROL,KEYCODE_MINUS
 22600 mark lagrange-shooter-2
 23000 tap 10 KEYCODE_Q
 23800 mark ball-3-over-game-over
 25000 mark attract-after-game

# ---- the service menu --------------------------------------------------------
 25400 tap 12 KEYCODE_7
 26000 mark service-menu-open
 26200 tap 12 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
 26500 tap 12 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
 26800 tap 12 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
 27300 mark service-record-3-technical
 27600 tap 12 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
 27900 tap 12 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
 28400 mark service-record-selected
 29000 tap 12 KEYCODE_7
 29600 mark service-menu-closed
 30400 mark end
